IMPORT prelude

-- Goods and Services Tax Voucher Fund Act 2012 (Singapore) -- who the Fund may help and on what footing (ss 4(1)(a), 8A), how a
-- payment out of the Fund is authorised (s 6), the sharing and confidentiality of information about applicants (ss 9, 10), the
-- recovery of overpayments (s 11), the Fund's financial year (s 12), the offences an applicant can commit and their punishment
-- (ss 10(2), 16, 17, 19(2)(c)), and composition (s 18). The net-income rule for the Fund's investments (s 3(4)) is included as
-- the Act's only other arithmetic.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 9/3/2025), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/GSTVFA2012.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December
-- 2021"; the one later amendment annotated is Act 5 of 2025 wef 09/03/2025 (s 8(2), (2A)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0076 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The answer the text gives is: very little directly. The Act creates the Fund and leaves who gets a GST Voucher,
-- and how much, to regulations (s 19(2)(a)) and to "a public scheme" that is not in the deposit. SCOPED accordingly to the parts
-- a recipient or applicant actually meets. Not encoded: the moneys paid into the Fund (s 3(2)), expenses (s 5), dissolution
-- (s 7), the Minister's responsibility and appointments (s 8, including the Gazette requirement in s 8(2A)), accounts, audit and
-- presentation to Parliament (ss 13 to 15), and any regulation or scheme made under the Act (none was retrieved). No voucher
-- amount or eligibility test appears in this row because none appears in the Act.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Goods and Services Tax Voucher Fund Act 2012 -- assistance`

§§ `4(1)(a) and 8A -- who may be helped, and on what footing`

-- s 4(1)(a): moneys may be applied "to provide financial assistance (including cash grants, grants-in-aid, rebates, reliefs,
-- subsidies and credits) under a public scheme to such natural persons as may be prescribed, in order to mitigate the impact of
-- the goods and services tax on their living expenses". [19/2020]
-- s 8A: "No person has an absolute right to any financial assistance under a public scheme using moneys from the Fund." [19/2020]
GIVEN `is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN, `is of a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Fund may assist the person` IF
    `is a natural person` AND `is of a prescribed class`

GIVEN `is eligible under the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has an absolute right to the assistance` IF
    FALSE

§§ `6 -- payments out of the Fund`

-- s 6(1): "Moneys must not be withdrawn from the Fund unless they are charged upon the Fund or are authorised to be withdrawn or
-- transferred under this Act." (2): "A payment must not be made out of the Fund unless the payment is approved by the Minister or a
-- person authorised, in writing, by the Minister."
GIVEN `is charged upon the Fund or authorised under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `approved by a person the Minister authorised in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment may be made` IF
        `is charged upon the Fund or authorised under this Act`
    AND (`approved by the Minister` OR `approved by a person the Minister authorised in writing`)

§§ `9 -- information shared to pay assistance`

-- s 9(1): where the Minister "certifies that it is necessary" for an appointed body to have another public authority's
-- confidential information in order to disburse assistance, (a) the Minister responsible for that other authority "may ...
-- direct" it to provide the information, and (b) it "must comply with the direction ... whether or not it is under any
-- obligation ... not to disclose the information".
-- (2): no offence, breach of confidence or civil liability "by virtue merely of the person disclosing any information in accordance
-- with any direction".
-- (3): "Nothing in this section applies to any document, information, return and assessment to which section 6 of the Income Tax
-- Act 1947 applies."
GIVEN `the Minister certified it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the responsible Minister directed disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is income tax information under s 6 of the Income Tax Act 1947` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the other public authority must disclose` IF
        `the Minister certified it necessary`
    AND `the responsible Minister directed disclosure`
    AND (NOT `is income tax information under s 6 of the Income Tax Act 1947`)

§§ `10 -- confidentiality of information about applicants`

-- s 10(1): an appointed body holding confidential information obtained "pursuant to a direction under section 9(1) ... must not
-- disclose the information to any other person unless the disclosure -- (a) is made with the written consent of the person to whom
-- the information relates; or (b) is for the purpose of the administration or enforcement of this Act."
-- (2): a contravention is an offence, "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ...
-- both".
GIVEN `obtained the information under a s 9(1) direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disclosed it to another person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person concerned consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `was for administering or enforcing this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence under s 10` IF
        `obtained the information under a s 9(1) direction`
    AND `disclosed it to another person`
    AND (NOT `the person concerned consented in writing`)
    AND (NOT `was for administering or enforcing this Act`)

§§ `11 -- recovery of overpayments`

-- s 11(a): where money is paid "to a person as financial assistance under a public scheme and the person is not eligible under the
-- public scheme to any financial assistance or is eligible for financial assistance of a lower amount ... the amount that has been
-- paid or paid in excess (as the case may be) is recoverable as a debt due to the Government."
-- An ineligible person is modelled as eligible for 0, so the whole payment is recoverable.
GIVEN `amount paid` IS A NUMBER, `amount the person was eligible for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount recoverable as a debt` IS
    IF `amount paid` > `amount the person was eligible for`
    THEN `amount paid` - `amount the person was eligible for`
    ELSE 0

§§ `12 -- financial year`

-- s 12: "The financial year of the Fund begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
-- Returned: the calendar year in which the financial year containing the given month began.
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the financial year begins in` IS
    IF `month` >= 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` - 1

§§ `16 -- false statements and documents in an application`

-- s 16: any person who, "in relation to any application (whether by the person or on behalf of another) to a public authority or
-- person appointed under section 8(2) for any financial assistance from the Fund or for the purpose of obtaining any financial
-- assistance from the Fund -- (a) knowingly or recklessly makes any false statement; or (b) produces or provides or causes or
-- knowingly allows to be produced or provided any document which the person knows to be false in a material particular", is guilty
-- of an offence: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both".
-- Recklessness is enough for a statement; a document needs knowledge AND a material falsity.
DECLARE `Conduct in an application` HAS
    `relates to an application for assistance from the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made a false statement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew the statement was false` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was reckless whether the statement was true` IS A BOOLEAN
    `produced or caused or allowed a document to be produced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the document is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew the document was false` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Conduct in an application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under s 16` IF
        `the conduct`'s `relates to an application for assistance from the Fund`
    AND (    (     `the conduct`'s `made a false statement`
               AND (`the conduct`'s `knew the statement was false` OR `the conduct`'s `was reckless whether the statement was true`))
          OR (     `the conduct`'s `produced or caused or allowed a document to be produced`
               AND `the conduct`'s `the document is false in a material particular`
               AND `the conduct`'s `knew the document was false`))

§§ `10(2), 16 and 19(2)(c) -- maximum punishment`

-- ss 10(2), 16: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both".
-- s 19(2)(c): regulations may make a contravention an offence "punishable with a fine not exceeding $5,000 or with imprisonment for
-- a term not exceeding 12 months or with both" -- a ceiling on what regulations may prescribe.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `an unauthorised disclosure under s 10`
    `a false statement or document under s 16`
    `a contravention of the regulations`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine in dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an unauthorised disclosure under s 10` THEN 5000
    WHEN `a false statement or document under s 16` THEN 5000
    WHEN `a contravention of the regulations` THEN 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an unauthorised disclosure under s 10` THEN 12
    WHEN `a false statement or document under s 16` THEN 12
    WHEN `a contravention of the regulations` THEN 12

§§ `17 -- officers and partners`

-- s 17(1): where an offence by a body corporate is proved "(a) to have been committed with the consent or connivance of an officer;
-- or (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the officer's part, the officer as well as the body corporate shall be guilty". (3)
-- and (4) say the same of partners and of officers of unincorporated associations; (5) "body corporate" includes a limited
-- liability partnership.
GIVEN `the body committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the officer consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the offence is attributable to the officer's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
        `the body committed an offence under this Act`
    AND (`the officer consented or connived` OR `the offence is attributable to the officer's neglect`)

§§ `18 -- composition`

-- s 18(1): a public officer authorised by the Minister "may compound any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding the lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum
-- fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $1,000." (2): on payment "no further proceedings are to be taken".
-- (3): the Minister prescribes the compoundable offences by regulations; none were retrieved.
GIVEN `is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `by a public officer the Minister authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded` IF
    `is prescribed as compoundable` AND `by a public officer the Minister authorised`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the lower of` IS
    IF `a` <= `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `prescribed maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum composition sum` IS
    `the lower of` (`prescribed maximum fine` / 2) 1000

§§ `3(4) -- net income from the Fund's investments`

-- s 3(4): "the net income from investments is the amount ascertained by adding to, or deducting from, the income received from
-- investments of moneys in the Fund any profit derived or loss sustained (as the case may be) from the realisation of the
-- investments."
GIVEN `income received` IS A NUMBER, `profit on realisation` IS A NUMBER, `loss on realisation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the net income from investments` IS
    `income received` + `profit on realisation` - `loss on realisation`
